StoppedVolumeEdit's attribute copy without XATTR_NOFOLLOW_ANY (macOS 13). macOS 11 ignores that bit, and getxattr
then follows a link in the path (checked on the Big Sur Mac), which on a device's volume could reach a file outside
it. Both files are opened with O_NOFOLLOW_ANY instead, which macOS 11 has and which makes a link anywhere in either
path ELOOP, and the attributes go through flistxattr, fgetxattr and fsetxattr on the descriptors. O_NONBLOCK keeps a
FIFO from blocking the open. DevicePath's O_SEARCH needs no change: macOS 11 opens a directory with it and openat
works through it.

